# No "* text=auto" here, unlike VL.NetTopologySuite: this repository has files committed with
# CRLF (the csproj, a script, twenty .vl) and one with mixed endings, and text=auto would turn
# the next edit of each into a whole-file diff. Only the files that fail silently are pinned.

# A .vl is a vvvv gamma document, and a corrupted one fails SILENTLY - vvvv simply does not load
# it, with no error anywhere. So its bytes are pinned rather than left to whatever core.autocrlf a
# contributor happens to have.
#
# "-text", not VL.NetTopologySuite's "text eol=crlf": every .vl here was already committed with
# CRLF in the index (git ls-files --eol, 2026-09-26), and "text" would renormalize all twenty of
# them to LF in one noisy commit. "-text" stores the bytes exactly as committed - BOM, CRLF and
# all - and git diff still shows them as text.
*.vl -text

# Same reasoning, same silent failure: Help.xml orders the help patches and carries their search
# tags, and vvvv ignores a malformed one without complaint.
Help.xml -text
